; ted-join-no-mforget2 (#365): Join freed the appended line without
; telling the label column (no mforget2).  Lines "a=1", ".loop:b=2",
; "c=3": the label column shows "loop".  Join on line 1: no line starts
; with a label any more.  Correct: the label column is rebuilt (no label:
; TED reopens its screen without it); the original keeps showing "loop",
; its node pointing to the freed line.  In the decoded dump the label
; column follows the cells of the prop gadget ("··", unknown cells):
; "·loop" is the label column, not the text of line 1.
; @fixed #365
; @file bo.bas "a=1\n.loop:b=2\nc=3\n"
; @source F bo.bas
; @expect screen before "loop"
; @expect noscreen joined "\xc2\xb7loop"
timeout 10
wait req "OKEE DOKEE"
gad 1
wait screen
dump before
menu 1 8
dump joined
menu 0 2
wait freq "Name to save file as"
freq ok
wait screen
menu 0 9
wait exit
